-- name    : RiemannRoch_IntrinsicAdeles
-- status  : Definition
-- author  : @Idealson
-- created : 2026-10-20T11:46:51.775978+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/1731a017-c7b5-44d7-828c-596213c9a504
-- title:
--   Intrinsic divisors and adeles of a function field, and pole divisors $(x)_\infty$
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $k$ is a field and $K$ is a field together with compatible embeddings $k[X]\subset k(X)\subset K$ such that $K/k(X)$ is a finite separable extension; $K$ is thus an algebraic function field in one variable over $k$, presented together with the transcendental element $x=X\in K$. Write $\mathcal O_\infty=\{f\in k(X):\deg f\le0\}$ for the valuation ring at infinity of $k(X)$ (with $\deg f=\deg(\text{numerator})-\deg(\text{denominator})$) and $\mathfrak m_\infty$ for its maximal ideal, $\mathcal O_K$ for the integral closure of $k[X]$ in $K$ and $\mathcal O_{K,\infty}$ for the integral closure of $\mathcal O_\infty$ in $K$. The *chart places* are the elements of $\mathbb P^{\mathrm{ch}}_K=\operatorname{Spec}^1(\mathcal O_K)\sqcup\operatorname{Spec}^1(\mathcal O_{K,\infty})$ (finite and infinite places), $v_P$ is the normalized $P$-adic valuation, $\deg P=\dim_k(\mathcal O/P)$ for the relevant Dedekind domain $\mathcal O$, and a chart divisor is a finitely supported $D:\mathbb P^{\mathrm{ch}}_K\to\mathbb Z$ with $\deg D=\sum_P D(P)\deg P$. Let $\mathcal A_K$, $\mathcal A_K(D)$ and $\widetilde K$ be the chart adele space, its filtration and the principal adeles (file `RiemannRoch_Adeles`), $\mathcal L(D)$, $\ell(D)$ the Riemann–Roch space and its dimension, and let $P\mapsto P^{\mathrm{int}}$ be the bijection from chart places to intrinsic places (valuation subrings $\mathcal O\subsetneq K$ containing $k$ with value group $\cong\mathbb Z$).
--
--   This file transfers the divisor and adele theory to intrinsic places and introduces pole divisors. It introduces:
--
--   1. **Comparison of local data.** $k$-algebra isomorphisms between the valuation ring of a chart place $P$ (the localization at $P$) and that of $P^{\mathrm{int}}$, and between their residue fields; hence $\deg P^{\mathrm{int}}=\deg P$.
--   2. **Intrinsic divisors.** $\operatorname{Div}(K)=\bigoplus_{Q}\mathbb Z\,Q$ over intrinsic places, its isomorphism with chart divisors induced by $P\mapsto P^{\mathrm{int}}$, the principal divisor $\operatorname{div}(x)$ of $x\in K^\times$ (transported from the chart one) and the degree $\deg D=\sum_Q D(Q)\deg Q$.
--   3. **Intrinsic adeles.** The adele space on intrinsic places (families $(\alpha_Q)$ in $K$, integral at almost all $Q$), a $K$-module, with its filtration $\mathcal A_K(D)=\{\alpha: v_Q(\alpha_Q)\ge-D(Q)\ \forall Q\}$ and diagonal; a $k$-linear isomorphism with the chart adele space which matches the filtrations, the diagonals and the sums $\mathcal A_K(D)+\widetilde K$.
--   4. **Pole divisors.** For $x\in K$, the chart pole divisor
--   $$(x)_\infty=\max\big(-\operatorname{div}(x),0\big),\qquad (0)_\infty=0,$$
--   and for a finite family $(f_i)$ the bound $B=\sum_i(f_i)_\infty$.
--   5. **The chart variable.** The element $x_K\in K$, image of $X\in k(X)$, and the subfield $k(x)\subseteq K$ generated by an element $x$.
--
--   It also contains the structural lemmas needed below: powers $1,x,\dots,x^r$ of an element transcendental over $k$ are linearly independent; $(x)_\infty\ge0$; if $x\ne0$ is not algebraic over $k$ then $v_P(x)<0$ for some chart place and $\deg(x)_\infty>0$; $x^n\in\mathcal L(n\,(x)_\infty)$, $f_i\,x^j\in\mathcal L(B+r\,(x)_\infty)$ for $j\le r$; $x_K$ is transcendental over $k$; for a basis $b_1,\dots,b_n$ of $K/k(X)$ the products $b_i x_K^j$ are $k$-linearly independent, so that $n(r+1)\le\ell(B+r\,(x_K)_\infty)$; an elementary inequality ($n(r+1)\le dr+c$ for all $r$ implies $n\le d$); and, when $k$ is the full constant field,
--   $$[K:k(X)]\le\deg\,(x_K)_\infty .$$
--
--   Intrinsic divisors and adeles are the setting of the final, coordinate-free statements; the pole divisor of $x_K$ is the tool for proving that the genus is finite. In the chain of definition files it imports `RiemannRoch_Adeles` and is imported by `RiemannRoch_GenusCharts`.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The function field is not constructed from $k$: $K$ is an arbitrary field carrying the instances `Algebra k[X] K`, `Algebra k⟮X⟯ K`, `IsScalarTower k[X] k⟮X⟯ K`, Mathlib's `FunctionField k K` (i.e. $K$ is finite-dimensional over $k(X)$) and `Algebra.IsSeparable k⟮X⟯ K`; when constants are needed, also `Algebra k K` with `IsScalarTower k k[X] K`. Intrinsic divisors are `FunctionField.Divisor k K := Place k K →₀ ℤ`, with `divisorEquivChart : DivisorA k K ≃+ Divisor k K` (`Finsupp.domCongr chartToPlace`), `FunctionField.principalDivisor` and `Divisor.deg`. The intrinsic adele space is `FunctionField.AdeleSpace k K`, with `adeleEquivChart : AdeleSpace k K ≃ₗ[k] Chart.AdeleSpace k K`. The pole divisor is `FunctionField.Chart.polarDivisor`, the bound is `basisPoleBound`, $x_K$ is `XK k K` and $k(x)$ is `rationalSubfield` (Mathlib's `IntermediateField.adjoin k {x}`). The last inequality is stated with `Module.finrank k⟮X⟯ K` and assumes `IsFullConstantField k K`. Valuations take values in $\mathbb Z_{m0}=\{0\}\cup\{\exp(n):n\in\mathbb Z\}$, written multiplicatively, so that the Lean valuation of $f\ne0$ at $P$ is $\exp(-v_P(f))$; the inequality $\exp(-v_P(f))\le\exp(D(P))$ is the additive condition $v_P(f)\ge -D(P)$.
-- source:
--   H. Stichtenoth, *Algebraic Function Fields and Codes*, 2nd ed., GTM 254, Springer 2009, Section 1.4 (divisors, degree, pole divisor $(x)_\infty$, cf. Theorem 1.4.11 $\deg(x)_\infty=[F:K(x)]$) and Section 1.5 (adeles). Lean: riemann-roch-function-fields by Guanghao Li (Apache 2.0), ported to Mathlib 0df444a: https://github.com/vaca22/riemann-roch-function-fields/blob/dbca5beed1da77e2ecd1eec207d0451fa57e8aa6/RiemannRoch/CoordinateFree/Divisor.lean, https://github.com/vaca22/riemann-roch-function-fields/blob/dbca5beed1da77e2ecd1eec207d0451fa57e8aa6/RiemannRoch/CoordinateFree/AdeleSpace.lean, https://github.com/vaca22/riemann-roch-function-fields/blob/dbca5beed1da77e2ecd1eec207d0451fa57e8aa6/RiemannRoch/Genus/Polar.lean

